# SPA fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The site uses browser history, not hash history, so `/work` is a URL the
# static host has no file for. Without this line it answers 404 — and it answers
# it on the one visit nobody tests locally: the second one, arriving from
# somebody else's link, or from a refresh. 200 rather than 301/302 because the
# path must survive to the client for the router to match it.
#
# Vercel reads `vercel.json` at the repo root instead and ignores this file.
# GitHub Pages reads neither and needs a copied `404.html`.
/*    /index.html   200
